Guard MailerPass against autoload fatals from orphan decorators

MailerPass::process() runs at TYPE_BEFORE_OPTIMIZATION, before Symfony's
DecoratorServicePass removes service decorators whose inner service is
absent (`decoration_on_invalid: ignore`). When such a decorator's class
file references symbols from a disabled module, the autoload triggered
by class_exists() fatals and crashes container compile.

Reproduction on this site: `history` is enabled without `comment`;
history.services.yml registers `history.comment_link_builder` decorating
`comment.link_builder`, and HistoryCommentLinkBuilder implements
`Drupal\comment\CommentLinkBuilderInterface`.

See https://www.drupal.org/project/symfony_mailer/issues/3589038 and
merge request !220 (upstream, not yet released as of symfony_mailer 2.0.2).

